{"v":2,"s":"c","w":7,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Oxides","b":"<p><b>Oxides</b> (oksidi) are compounds of an element with oxygen.</p><ul><li><b>Metal oxides are basic</b>: with water they give bases. CaO + H₂O → Ca(OH)₂.</li><li><b>Nonmetal oxides are acidic</b>: with water they give acids. SO₃ + H₂O → H₂SO₄.</li></ul><p>Names: Na₂O natrijum-oksid, Fe₂O₃ gvožđe(III)-oksid, CO₂ ugljenik(IV)-oksid (ugljen-dioksid).</p>"},{"t":"read","h":"Acids and bases","b":"<p><b>Acids</b> (kiseline) are H + an acid residue:</p><table class=\"mini\"><tr><td>HCl</td><td>hlorovodonična</td></tr><tr><td>H₂SO₄</td><td>sumporna</td></tr><tr><td>H₂SO₃</td><td>sumporasta</td></tr><tr><td>HNO₃</td><td>azotna</td></tr><tr><td>H₂CO₃</td><td>ugljena</td></tr><tr><td>H₃PO₄</td><td>fosforna</td></tr></table><p><b>Bases</b> (baze, hidroksidi) are a metal + OH groups: NaOH natrijum-hidroksid, Ca(OH)₂ kalcijum-hidroksid.</p>"},{"t":"read","h":"Salts","b":"<p><b>Salts</b> (soli) are a metal (or NH₄) + an acid residue. The ending tells you the acid:</p><ul><li><b>-id</b>: no oxygen — NaCl natrijum-hlorid, FeS₂ gvožđe-disulfid</li><li><b>-at</b>: from the “-na” acid — sulfat, nitrat, karbonat, fosfat</li><li><b>-it</b>: from the “-sta” acid, one O fewer — sulfit, nitrit</li><li><b>hidrogen-</b>: acid salts — NaHCO₃ natrijum-hidrogenkarbonat</li></ul><div class=\"callout\">Like surnames: “-at” and “-it” tell you the family the way “-ić” tells you a surname is Serbian.</div><div class=\"callout geo\">Minerals are mostly salts and oxides: calcite CaCO₃, gypsum CaSO₄·2H₂O, halite NaCl, pyrite FeS₂.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 184\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How the families connect: metals give basic oxides and bases, nonmetals give acidic oxides and acids, and acid + base gives a salt and water.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><rect x=\"4\" y=\"8\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Metal</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\">Ca</text><rect x=\"112\" y=\"8\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"157\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Basic oxide</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\">CaO</text><rect x=\"238\" y=\"8\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"277\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Base</text><text x=\"277\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"10\">Ca(OH)₂</text><rect x=\"4\" y=\"70\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Nonmetal</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"10\">S</text><rect x=\"112\" y=\"70\" width=\"90\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"157\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Acidic oxide</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"10\">SO₃</text><rect x=\"238\" y=\"70\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"277\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Acid</text><text x=\"277\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"10\">H₂SO₄</text><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"27\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"27\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"93\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"9\">+O₂</text><line x1=\"202\" y1=\"27\" x2=\"236\" y2=\"27\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"219\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"9\">+H₂O</text><line x1=\"76\" y1=\"89\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"89\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"93\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\">+O₂</text><line x1=\"202\" y1=\"89\" x2=\"236\" y2=\"89\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"219\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\">+H₂O</text><rect x=\"96\" y=\"140\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" class=\"sf\"/><text x=\"166\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">Salt + water</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"10\">CaSO₄ + H₂O</text><line x1=\"276\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"214\" y2=\"138\" class=\"kc\" marker-end=\"url(#ahc)\"/><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"226\" y2=\"138\" class=\"kc\" marker-end=\"url(#ahc)\"/></svg><figcaption>How the families connect: metals give basic oxides and bases, nonmetals give acidic oxides and acids, and acid + base gives a salt and water.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"ex","q":"Name K₂SO₄, and write the formula of kalcijum-nitrat.","s":["K₂SO₄: metal kalijum + SO₄ (from sumporna kiselina) → kalijum-sulfat.","Kalcijum-nitrat: Ca is II, NO₃ is I.","Cross: Ca(NO₃)₂."],"a":"kalijum-sulfat; Ca(NO₃)₂"},{"t":"mc","q":"Na₂CO₃ is:","o":["natrijum-karbonat","natrijum-karbid","natrijum-hidrogenkarbonat","natrijum-oksid"],"a":0,"e":"CO₃ comes from ugljena kiselina → karbonat."},{"t":"mc","q":"HNO₃ is:","o":["hlorovodonična kiselina","azotna kiselina","fosforna kiselina","azotasta kiselina"],"a":1,"e":"HNO₃ — azotna; HNO₂ would be azotasta."},{"t":"mc","q":"Which is a base?","o":["HCl","KOH","CO₂","NaCl"],"a":1,"e":"Metal + OH group."},{"t":"mc","q":"CaO + H₂O → ?","o":["CaH₂","Ca(OH)₂","CaCO₃","H₂CaO₂ acid"],"a":1,"e":"A metal oxide with water gives a base."},{"t":"mc","q":"Salts of sumporasta kiselina (H₂SO₃) are called:","o":["sulfati","sulfidi","sulfiti","sulfoni"],"a":2,"e":"-sta acid → -it salt."}]}